Looking at the error, the issue is in `print_response`: when parsing answer records, the CLASS field (2 bytes) between TYPE and TTL was not accounted for. This caused TTL, RDLENGTH, and RDATA to be read at wrong offsets, producing garbage values and eventually an out-of-bounds access.

The DNS RR format after the NAME is: TYPE(2) + **CLASS(2)** + TTL(4) + RDLENGTH(2) + RDATA(variable). The original code skipped CLASS, reading TTL from `next+2` instead of `next+4`, RDLENGTH from `next+6` instead of `next+8`, and RDATA from `next+8` instead of `next+10`.

